{"id":"5ae54eda51ea48c98085244c75ac3ea8","owner":"Province.Of.British.Columbia","created":1553035249000,"modified":1693409357000,"guid":null,"name":null,"title":"Contaminated Sites Regulation - Natural Wildlands Land Use","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service"],"description":"<p><b>Purpose<\/b>: This data set was developed to present the spatial extent of areas identified as Natural Wildlands land use on a single map.  This map will be used by responsible persons and other interested stakeholders to determine if a specific contaminated site is identified as Natural Wildlands land use under the Contaminated Sites Regulation.<\/p><p><b>Notes<\/b>: Areas identified as Natural Wildlands land use for purposes of the Contaminated Sites Regulation (CSR).  Areas identified in this data set are designated protected areas identified in Schedule 2.1 of the CSR and represent areas protected for the primary purpose of supporting natural ecosystems.  These areas are afforded the highest level of protection under the CSR.<\/p><p><b>WMS GetCapabilities URL<\/b>: DataBC also offers access to this data in OGC WMS format.  WMS is useful when the map author does not require custom popups, styling, or analytic capabilities for the layer.  ArcGIS Online authors may want to use WMS, instead of this ArcGIS Server layer, in the following scenarios:<br /> <li>Where they want to use existing Data Custodian approved styling, and/or <\/li><li>They only need simple identify and map rendering functionality.<\/li><br />Copy the: <a href='https://openmaps.gov.bc.ca/geo/pub/WHSE_ENVIRONMENT_ASSESSMENT.CSR_NATURAL_WILDLANDS_SP/ows?service=WMS&request=GetCapabilities' rel='nofollow ugc'>WMS GetCapabilities URL<\/a> to add this web item to an ArcGIS Online Map or Scene Viewer.  In some cases, multiple Styles are listed in the GetCapabilities and can be added as WMS Custom parameters. For more information on how to use a WMS layer see - <a href='https://doc.arcgis.com/en/arcgis-online/reference/ogc.htm' rel='nofollow ugc'>ESRI's OGC ArcGIS Online Help<\/a><\/p><br /><p><b>BC Data Catalogue Metadata URL<\/b>: <a href='https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/6c5f8176-9f99-4ecb-b681-23aba1946647' rel='nofollow ugc'>https://catalogue.data.gov.bc.ca/dataset/6c5f8176-9f99-4ecb-b681-23aba1946647<\/a><\/p>","tags":["contaminated sites","natural wildlands","remediation"],"snippet":"Areas identified as Natural Wildlands land use for purposes of the Conta...","thumbnail":"thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-140.96,46.1411],[-109.236,62.0882]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":null,"accessInformation":"Environmental Emergencies and Land Remediation","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p>The data set provided by this web service is licensed under <a href='https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content?id=1AAACC9C65754E4D89A118B875E0FBDA' rel='nofollow ugc'>Access Only<\/a><\/p>\n  <p>The B.C. Map Hub and associated materials, including map applications (&quot;Maps&quot;), trade-marks and official marks (collectively, &quot;Materials&quot;), are owned or used under license by the Province of British Columbia (&quot;Province&quot;) and are protected by copyright and trade-mark laws.  Please see the <a href='https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content?id=14CE6DD7756F402287618963D936BE44' rel='nofollow ugc'>Disclaimer<\/a> for further details.<\/p>\n  <p>The Province does not collect, use or disclose personal information through the ArcGIS Online website.  Please be aware, however, that IP addresses are collected by Esri and are stored on Esri's servers located outside of Canada.  For further information, including the purposes for which your IP address is collected,  please see Esri's Privacy Policy at:  <a href='https://www.esri.com/legal/privacy' rel='nofollow ugc'>https://www.esri.com/legal/privacy<\/a>.   By accessing or using the B.C. Map Hub, you consent, effective as of the date of such access or use, to Esri storing and accessing your IP address outside of Canada for the purposes described in Esri's Privacy Policy.  Should you have any questions about the collection of your IP address, please contact BCGov AGOL CONTACT at Data@gov.bc.ca, PO BOX 9864 STN PROV GOVT, Victoria BC  V8W 9T5<\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://maps.gov.bc.ca/arcgis/rest/services/whse/bcgw_pub_whse_environment_assessment/MapServer/1","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":73,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":7548,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"ubm4tcTYICKBpist","scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"contentOrigin":"self","lastViewed":1766008800000,"portalUrl":"https://governmentofbc.maps.arcgis.com/sharing"}